  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Drier weather, featuring cool overnights and \nwarm afternoons.\n\nClear skies and subsidence around the back side of a coastal \nlow is enhancing dry layer with surface dewpoints in the 30s. A \nfew locations have slipped into the upper 20s which suggests \nonce we decouple this evening temperatures should take a \nsubstantial nose dive after sunset. GFS-Based Coop guidance \nsuggests some of our normally colder locations may be cold \nenough for some patchy frost late tonight...places like Burkes \nGarden VA, White Sulphur Springs WV, and Jefferson NC. Not\nenough to warrant an advisory.  \n\nClear skies are expected to persist into Saturday with a much \ndrier airmass now in place over the region...yielding a \nbeautiful fall day. Strong surface low over the Atlantic will \ncontinue to strengthen and move north through Sunday morning. \nModel guidance does indicate that the low may retrograde west on\nSunday and stall along the New Jersey coast through Monday. \nThis appears to be close enough to bring some cloudiness to the \nforecast area on Sunday and Monday. Have also added a mention of\nshowers along the I64 corridor given enough guidance showing \nsome potential for showers to reach the area.\n\nLow pressure will lift north and weaken by Tuesday as high\npressure then begins to build over the eastern CONUS. Should see\nincreasingly warmer temperatures through next week given\nincreasing heights and return flow. Other than some isolated\nshowers Sun/Mon, dry conditions will likely continue through at\nleast Thursday next week.",
